🚀 Day 41 – GitHub Actions Triggers & Matrix Builds

Today I learned different ways to trigger GitHub Actions workflows and how to run the same workflow across multiple environments using Matrix Builds.

📚 What I Learned

- ✅ Pull Request Trigger ("pull_request")
- ✅ Scheduled Trigger ("schedule" with cron)
- ✅ Manual Trigger ("workflow_dispatch")
- ✅ Matrix Builds for multiple Python versions
- ✅ Running jobs in parallel
- ✅ Excluding specific matrix combinations
- ✅ "fail-fast: true" vs "fail-fast: false"

🛠️ Workflows Created

- "pr-check.yml"
- "schedule.yml"
- "manual.yml"
- "matrix.yml"

Key Takeaways

- Pull Request workflows help automate code checks before merging.
- Scheduled workflows run automatically using cron expressions.
- Manual workflows can be started from the Actions tab with custom inputs.
- Matrix builds save time by testing the same workflow on multiple environments simultaneously.

Every day I'm getting more comfortable with GitHub Actions and CI/CD concepts.

